## PAGE-END (E2) AND THE OTHER STANDING PROPERTIES: re-measured at the base and at your head, by program
**Property:** at your head, in every cell of the gate's page-end frame, (a) `ref.scrollHeight - head.scrollHeight` is at most 64 (over 64: 0 cells), and its maximum is no larger than the BASE's maximum read by the same instrument in the same run (the gate read 48 at the visual round's head); a page that got TALLER only lowers that figure; (b) Shift+Tab up the open menu from the page's end: 0 page moves; (c) the footer is never under the open menu: 0 covered; (d) the band under the menu at the page's end is at most 72 px; (e) header 72 px in every cell of `hdr.cjs` (4 roles x widths x rail states); (f) widths 228 / 64 / 245, footer 252 / 88; (g) no horizontal scroll at 390, 768, 1024, 1280, 1440 and 1920. **At least:** the instruments are the gate's `ring1289.cjs` (172 lines, `.tools/b1289/ring/`, the 72-cell page-end frame against the old-UAT reference `69338b64`: READ and COPY, never run in place) and the visual round's `pageend.cjs` (24 lines, the 84 cells), `carrier.cjs` (18 lines, run at 800 AND 500 px high; the 500 px frame is the one that sees short pages) and `hdr.cjs` (`.tools/b1285/scratch/`), all MEASURED to exist at drafting. Controls: a floor plant of 80 px reads different in more than 0 cells; the base run reproduces the gate's figures (page-end max 48, over 64 0 of 72) or the difference is printed, not hidden. **Any other shape of the property: prove it meets it or STOP.** A built line whose build breaks (a)-(g) is reverted to KEEP with the cell and the px printed (a finding, never tuned to a sub-pixel offset by a compensating margin).
**Heights are reported, not forbidden:** per T line print the carrier-frame change of `scrollHeight` per route (grouped counts; the gate's `rows2.cjs` / `rows3.cjs` method, `.tools/b1280/g/`: inject, read, selector match count above 0 before every read, a read on a zero match is void) so the product owner can see what moved.

## CONTRAST, WORDS, FLOORS: by program
- **Contrast:** every NEW colour pair is added to `TOKEN_PAIRS` and `contrast.test.ts` passes (text 4.5, non-text 3; no threshold touched). Drafter's figures (MEASURED, python 3 `-I -B`, controls printed first: black on white 21.00, `#767676` on white 4.54, `#c05000` on white 4.78): T04 icon `#0089ca` on `#e8f6ff` 3.51; T08 `#0a2940` on white 14.96; T13 `#ca5d4e` on white 4.05; T12 / T13 `#d47f27` 3.06 and `#47a389` 3.06; T18 white on `#173c55` 11.58. T14's state pairs you measure. A pair under its floor is a finding printed in STATUS, not a loosened threshold.
- **Words:** words changed 0. The crawl (`crawl2.cjs`, 307 routes, 3 roles) is text-equal base vs head on every route, apart from any elapsed-time figure (name it); link names and hrefs 307 of 307; `axe` (`color-contrast` + 15 aria rules) 0 new violations in the visual round's 24 cells (copy `axe.cjs`). The added markup is exactly: the optional `aria-hidden` icon of T04. Nothing else adds an element, prop, hook, handler, data, route or word.
